_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past tense and Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.</br> The Past Continuous talks about a longer 'background' action.</br> The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when</span> and <span class=\"strong\">while</span> before the longer action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Susan called me while I was making dinner.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Dave wrote his essay while watching TV.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nonetheless", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in spite of what has just been said", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Don't get me wrong, I always like to see the Red Sox win but it was a great hit by Toronto, nonetheless.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about sports.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "inning", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one of the nine parts of a game in which each team bats", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You weren't looking too well after the ninth inning.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "traitor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is not loyal to his or her own country, friends, or team", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You'll sound like a traitor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "league", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a group of sports teams that play against each other", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I was thinking about joining the local baseball league.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "meringue", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sweet, whipped egg whites used as a topping for a dessert", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Alright then ... pass me some of that lemon meringue pie!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "coming down with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "feeling the start of a sickness", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Maybe you're coming down with something.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le15ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Silent UE", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Some letter combinations in the English language are silent. For example, when <span class=\"strong\">\"ue\"</span> is after a <span class=\"strong\">\"g\"</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">\"q\"</span> at the end of a word, it is usually silent.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When a word ends with <span class=\"strong\">-gue</span>, it makes a <span class=\"strong\">\"g\"</span> sound.<br><span class=\"italic\">For example: <ul><li>dialo<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li><li>lea<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li><li>fati<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When a word ends with <span class=\"strong\">-que</span>, it makes a <span class=\"strong\">\"k\"</span> sound.<br> <span class=\"italic\">For example:<br><ul><li>anti<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li><li>bis<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li><li>uni<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li></ul></span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes a <span class=\"strong\">\"ue\"</span> combination is silent in the middle of a word.<br><span class=\"italic\">For example:<br><ul><li>vag<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ly</li><li>uniq<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ness</li><li>antiq<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ness</li></ul></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'm feeling a little fatigued.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I was thinking about joining the local baseball league.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Research baseball in your city or country. Is it or was it a popular sport? Write 1 sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Is there a league? How many teams play in the league? Write 2 sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What types of injuries or health problems do you think baseball players get? Write 2 sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Present the information to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I complete research on a sport. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write 2 sentences about baseball leagues.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about the health problems of baseball players.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I present the information to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type":